  "query_preview": "Forecast Discussion...\n\nLooking past the holiday weekend, the upper flow pattern across NOAM \nlooks to feature continued blocking across Canada with a very strong \nPacific jet pushing systems into California and then into the \ncentral US.  850mb temp anomalies for the next couple of weeks show \nno cold air building in Canada, though some transient cold shots \nlook to move across NOAM with systems.  Some of the heavy lifting \nfor cold may have to be done by the parade of Pacific systems \nbringing modified cold into the western CONUS and then pushing it \neast.  Certainly not a cold/traditional Arctic airmass by any means. \nThe strong subtropical jet will continue as strong convection \ncontinues along the equator leading to strong latent heat release \nand increasing the thermal gradient (and thus the STJ) between the \nmid-latitudes and the equator.  Teleconnection pattern shows this \nrather well with a continued -AO/-NAO/+PNA pattern.  The fly in the \nointment for cold remains the EPO.  While the EPO is negative now, \nwe're going to see the resultant chill in the days leading up to \nThanksgiving.  Beyond that, the models take the EPO back to \nneutral/positive into early December.  There continues to be a \nsignal that we could see the EPO drop a bit into mid-December. \nRecent model performance hasn't been all that great with the \npredictability of the EPO (about 6-8 day lead time), but there have \nbeen subtle hints in previous ensemble runs that may help us key in \nmore potential cold in the weeks ahead.",
